# Progress Table Knowledge Base

> Scope: paginated Progress Table rendering for randomized and custom race
> tracks in the DLL.

---

## Overview

RVGL's original Progress Table only renders the first 14 race rows. The
randomizer replaces that draw path with a paginated renderer so the first page
keeps the original Progress Table behavior, while later pages expose all active
custom race tracks.

The implementation is display-only:

- It does not change save formats.
- It does not alter track progress flags.
- It does not alter unlock logic.
- Page state is runtime-only.

The main implementation lives in:

- `DLL/Mods/ProgressTableHooks.cpp`
- `DLL/Mods/ProgressTableHooks.h`

The hook is registered from:

- `DLL/Core/HookManager.cpp`

---

## Ghidra Findings

The original function:

| Symbol | Address |
| --- | ---: |
| `DrawProgressTable` | `0x00554870` |
| RVA | `0x00154870` |

Ghidra showed that the original renderer hard-codes the displayed race rows to
track indices `0..13`, stopping at `0xe`.

The game already has runtime track access through `GetTrackInfo(index)`.
Runtime indices are used as follows:

| Range | Meaning |
| ---: | --- |
| `0..20` | Vanilla track slots |
| `21..trackCount-1` | Custom/runtime tracks |

The Progress Table implementation intentionally skips vanilla special slots
`14..20` and uses only race-eligible custom tracks on custom pages.

---

## Files Changed

### New Module

`DLL/Mods/ProgressTableHooks.cpp`

Owns the replacement Progress Table renderer, pagination, cache rebuilds,
footer rendering, and left/right page handling.

`DLL/Mods/ProgressTableHooks.h`

Exposes runtime helpers:

- `ResetProgressTablePage()`
- `ClampProgressTablePage()`
- `InvalidateProgressTableCache()`

### Hook Registration

`DLL/Core/HookManager.cpp`

Registers a MinHook detour for:

```cpp
RVA_DRAW_PROGRESS_TABLE
```

The detour target is:

```cpp
Hook_DrawProgressTable
```

### Address Declarations

`DLL/Core/Addresses.h`

Adds RVAs used by the renderer:

| RVA constant | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `RVA_DRAW_PROGRESS_TABLE` | Original Progress Table draw function |
| `RVA_TRACK_LOAD_PROGRESS_FROM_FILE` | Loads track progress before rendering icons |
| `RVA_MENU_ACTION` | Reads current frontend left/right action |
| `RVA_LOCALE_STRINGS_PTR` | Reads localized UI strings |
| `RVA_GALLERY_SLOTS_PTR` | Reuses original frontend slot positioning data |
| `RVA_DRAW_TEXTURED_QUAD` | Draws panel and icon textures |
| `RVA_TRACK_IS_AVAILABLE_FOR_FRONTEND` | Preserves original availability behavior |

### RVGL Function Wrappers

`DLL/Game/RVGLFunctions.h`

`DLL/Game/RVGLFunctions.cpp`

Expose function pointers for RVGL helpers needed by the replacement renderer,
including progress loading, drawing, UTF-8 visible character counting, and
championship status checks.

### Runtime State

`DLL/Mods/RandomizerState.h`

Adds `ProgressTableRuntimeState` to `RandomizerContext`.

The state stores:

- current page
- cached stock page tracks
- cached custom page tracks
- cached runtime track count
- cache validity

### Cache Reset Points

`DLL/Mods/ProfileHooks.cpp`

Resets the current page on profile load.

`DLL/Mods/TrackHooks.cpp`

Invalidates and clamps the Progress Table cache after vanilla and custom track
loading.

### Build Integration

`DLL/CMakeLists.txt`

Adds `Mods/ProgressTableHooks.cpp` to the DLL build.

---

## Pagination Rules

The renderer uses two different page layouts.

### Page 1

Page 1 preserves the original Progress Table layout:

- 14 race rows.
- Original cup grouping rows.
- Original localized cup names.
- Original Stunt Arena footer placement.
- Existing CupDC/Rooftops availability behavior.

The page size is:

```cpp
kStockRowsPerPage = 14;
```

### Custom Pages

Pages after page 1 show custom runtime race tracks:

- Runtime indices `21..GetRuntimeTrackCount()-1`.
- Only existing tracks.
- Only race-eligible tracks.
- No cup/difficulty grouping rows.
- Tracks sorted alphabetically.
- 21 tracks per page.

The page size is:

```cpp
kCustomRowsPerPage = 21;
```

The total page count is:

```text
1 + ceil(customRaceTrackCount / 21)
```

Page 1 is always present. If there are no custom race tracks, left/right page
controls do nothing.

---

## Track Selection

The cached track list is rebuilt by `RebuildProgressTableCache()`.

Page 1 is populated from the same first 14 randomized display slots used by the
original table.

Custom pages are populated by scanning runtime track indices starting at `21`.
The implementation filters out:

- missing track entries
- non-existing track entries
- battle/stunt/frontend-only entries
- vanilla special tracks

Custom tracks are sorted by display name so the extra pages are stable and easy
to scan.

---

## Performance

An early version rebuilt and sorted the custom track list while drawing the
Progress Table. With many custom tracks, that caused a visible lag spike when
opening the panel.

The current version caches the track lists in `ProgressTableRuntimeState`.

The cache is rebuilt only when:

- it is invalid
- the runtime track count changed

The cache is invalidated when track loading changes the runtime track set. The
current page is clamped after invalidation so it cannot point past the new page
count.

---

## Controls

The first control implementation patched a shared frontend menu descriptor.
That allowed page navigation, but it also broke unrelated left/right UI, such
as Yes/No dialogs.

The final implementation does not patch shared menu descriptors.

Instead, `Hook_DrawProgressTable()` reads `RVA_MENU_ACTION` only while the
Progress Table is being drawn.

Actions:

| Action | Meaning |
| ---: | --- |
| `2` | Previous page |
| `3` | Next page |

The page changes only when the target page is within bounds.

Because the action handling is scoped to the Progress Table draw hook, other
frontend panels keep their original left/right behavior.

---

## Rendering

The replacement renderer reuses RVGL's existing drawing helpers and localized
strings wherever possible.

It renders:

- panel background
- original localized column headers
- two-line Time Trial style headers
- original cup labels on page 1
- track rows
- progress icons
- Stunt Arena footer
- page counter

Custom pages intentionally do not render difficulty/cup labels. They display
only alphabetized custom race rows.

For custom pages, the layout leaves one blank row between the header area and
the first track row.

The Stunt Arena row is kept at the same vertical position as the original page.
On custom pages, this is achieved by using 21 track rows and leaving one blank
row between the final race row and the Stunt Arena footer.

The page counter is drawn in the bottom-right area, separate from the original
Stunt Arena text.

---

## Localization

User-visible labels are read from RVGL's locale string table through
`RVA_LOCALE_STRINGS_PTR`.

This applies to:

- cup labels such as `Bronze`, `Silver`, `Gold`, and `Platinum`
- Progress Table column labels
- Stunt Arena footer text

The Stunt Arena footer keeps the original game format. For example:

```text
Stunt Arena - Stars Collected: 0 of 20
```

The progress value portion remains green, matching the original behavior.

---

## Progress Loading

Before rendering a track row, the hook checks whether that track's progress is
loaded.

If `TRACKPROGRESS_PROGRESS_LOADED` is not set, it calls:

```cpp
Track_LoadProgressFromFile
```

This keeps progress icons correct for custom pages after restarting the game or
loading a profile.

The hook does not create new progress fields or rewrite save data.

---

## Important Implementation Points

`Hook_DrawProgressTable()`

Main detour. Handles page navigation, obtains visible tracks, draws the panel,
draws headers, draws track rows, and draws the footer.

`BuildVisibleTracksForPage()`

Returns the track rows visible on the current page. Page 1 uses stock rows;
custom pages use slices of the sorted custom track cache.

`GetProgressTablePageCount()`

Computes the current total page count from the cached custom track list.

`EnsureProgressLoaded()`

Loads progress for a track before its icons are rendered.

`DrawColumnHeaders()`

Draws the localized Progress Table column headers.

`DrawTrackRow()`

Draws one track row and its progress icons.

`DrawFooter()`

Draws the localized Stunt Arena footer and page counter.

---

## Test Expectations

### Exactly 14 randomized tracks

Expected behavior:

- Page 1 matches the original table.
- Page count is 1.
- Left/right controls do not change the page.

### More than 14 custom race tracks

Expected behavior:

- Page 1 shows the original randomized rows.
- Later pages show all custom race tracks.
- Custom pages are sorted alphabetically.
- Battle, stunt, and frontend-only tracks are not shown.

### Profile progress

Expected behavior:

- race win icons persist
- time trial icons persist
- reverse icons persist
- mirror icons persist
- practice star icons persist
- later custom pages still show progress after restart

### CupDC disabled

Expected behavior:

- Page 1 keeps the original availability behavior.
- The skipped Rooftops behavior remains unchanged.

### New or empty profile

Expected behavior:

- Opening the Progress Table does not crash.
- Missing progress files are handled by the existing RVGL progress loading path.

---

## Design Constraints

- Keep the feature display/navigation only.
- Keep page state runtime-only.
- Preserve original page 1 behavior.
- Use localized RVGL strings instead of hard-coded labels.
- Avoid shared frontend menu descriptor patches.
- Avoid rebuilding or sorting custom track lists during every draw.
- Keep the Stunt Arena footer aligned with the original page.
